--- /dev/null
+++ b/apps/zcode-cli/spec/machine-local-filesystem.md
@@ -0,0 +1,30 @@
+# Session filesystem scope
+
+The trusted session/create and session/resume caller may explicitly request
+`filesystemScope: "machine"`; omission means `workspace`. This is runtime-only
+policy, never inferred from model text or project configuration. Workspace identity
+continues to identify the project. A warm resume cannot change the scope; a cold
+resume must explicitly reauthorize it. Remote workspaces cannot opt in.
+
+Flow: trusted protocol request -> runtime config -> executor preflight -> existing
+permission broker -> handler. Machine scope requires reverse approval for Read,
+Write, Edit, Glob, Grep and Bash, even where edit mode would normally auto-allow.
+Plan denials take precedence. The broker still requires an active dispatch grant.
+
+Preflight canonicalizes existing ancestors, rejects network/device namespaces,
+Windows drive-relative paths, alternate streams, reserved device names and sensitive
+account paths. Workspace scope denies lexical or symlink traversal outside the root.
+Machine scope admits ordinary external local paths, including new files. Glob patterns
+cannot escape their validated search root. Successful Bash cwd changes may persist
+outside the workspace only in machine scope. Shell commands remain trusted local
+process execution, not an OS sandbox.
+
+Acceptance: sibling read/list/search only with machine scope; workspace defaults,
+plan mutations, traversal, symlink, network/device failures; unchanged reverse broker;
+explicit create/resume plumbing, build and cross-repository live canary. No credentials
+or account contents belong in diagnostics. Existing entitlement work is untouched.
+
+Machine-scope runtimes expose dedicated Glob/Grep tools, including after shell
+branch refresh. Embedded search must not remove local discovery from this surface.
+The host's Individual session admission supplies the same active dispatch grant
+as queued tasks; readonly admission never grants mutation or general shell use.
